  "id": "e17cdc6c-3e47-57e2-9915-7aa8a83b37d7",
  "slug": "jerk-chicken-egg-rolls-with-mango-habanero-sauce",
  "name": "Jerk Chicken Egg Rolls with Mango-Habanero Sauce",
  "recipe_type": "appetizer",
  "brief_description": "Jerk chicken, plantains, and cabbage are all wrapped up in these fusion egg rolls served with an easy homemade mango-habanero sauce.",
  "cuisine": "Caribbean",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "For the habanero sauce: Combine mango with 3/4 cup water, rice vinegar, garlic, and salt in a small saucepan. Add most of the brown sugar, reserving 1 teaspoon. Bring to a boil, then reduce heat to medium-low; cook for 5 minutes. Add habanero peppers and simmer for 2 minutes. Mix 2 tablespoon water with cornstarch; stir slurry into the saucepan. Cook over medium-high until thick, 3 to 5 minutes. Leave mixture chunky or blend for a smoother texture."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "For the filling: Heat 1 tablespoon oil in a large saucepan over medium-high heat. Add chicken thighs and saut\u00e9 until browned, 5 to 7 minutes; sprinkle jerk seasoning over chicken. Add shallot and garlic; cook and stir until shallot begins to soften, about 3 minutes. Reduce heat to medium; add cabbage, carrots, and reserved sugar. Cook until cabbage is translucent but still a little crunchy, 3 to 5 minutes. Taste for seasoning. Let mixture cool."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Heat remaining vegetable oil in a pan over medium-high heat. Fry plantains until they start to brown, about 5 minutes. Transfer plantains onto a paper towel and let cool."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Separate and place egg roll wrappers onto your work surface. Mix egg with water for egg wash."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "Lay out one wrapper with a corner pointed toward you. Use a slotted spoon to add some of the chicken and cabbage mixtures across the center. Sprinkle plantain bits on top. Use your finger or a pastry brush to lightly moisten edges of wonton wrappers with egg wash. Fold one corner of the wrapper over filling onto the opposite corner to form a triangle. Press edges together to seal. Fill and fold remaining egg rolls."
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "text": "Heat oil in a large saucepan over medium-high heat. Fry egg rolls in batches in hot oil, turning occasionally, until golden brown, about 5 minutes. Remove and drain on paper towels or a rack. Serve with mango-habanero sauce."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 18,
